            "observations": [
                "QWidget::grab() and QWidget::render() must be called on the GUI thread. Both are implemented by repainting the widget through QWidget::render(), so the call is synchronous and blocks the GUI thread for its duration.",
                "Neither call needs a current OpenGL context for raster widgets. A QWidget hierarchy that contains a QOpenGLWidget/D3D child is the case that needs a graphics context (see the openglwidget sample).",
                "Popups, QMenu and non-modal QDialog are separate top-level windows and are NOT part of a top-level widget capture. The target adapter must decide whether to share only the main window or to compose extra windows.",
                "Damage regions must be mapped into the shared target coordinate system before they are unioned. Child widgets report QPaintEvent::region() in their own coordinate system, so the tracker binds the top-level window widget as the shared target, translates each accepted child region with QWidget::mapTo() and clips it to the visible part of the ancestor chain.",
                "Storage identity (real backing-store address from QImage::constBits(), not QImage::cacheKey()): the reused producer target changed its pixel storage in 15 of 170 captures, and the address never moved on its own between captures (0 self-check hits). QImage uses implicit data sharing: QImage::detach() copies when the reference count is not 1, so a producer that published a shared QImage pays for a new allocation exactly on the captures where a consumer still held the previous frame. This is a copy-on-write semantic, not a fixed per-frame allocation rate: with no consumer holding a frame the same buffer is reused with no replacement at all.",
                "Storage-identity probe controls: the synthetic shared-write control relocated the storage in 170 of 170 runs (probe can detect a replacement), and the unique-write control kept the same address in 170 of 170 runs (the probe does not report phantom replacements).",
                "Storage-identity probe (real backing-store address from QImage::constBits(), not QImage::cacheKey()): 'QWidget::render() into reused QImage' probed 150 captures and replaced its pixel storage 15 times.",
                "Damage probe (mapped into the shared target coordinate system): 6600 paint events from the target subtree were accepted, 0 paint events were excluded because they belong to separate top-level windows or non-widget objects, and 0 mapped events fell outside the target rect. Application repaints covered 83.5 % of the shared target rect per frame on average, while the capture calls added 100.0 %. This is an observable child-region stream after mapping and clipping; it is not yet a transport-ready damage protocol."
            ],
